(89, 'Salem M. Ben-Zeglam', NULL, 3, 'Petroleum Engineering, Economics', 'Salem M. Ben-Zeglam,\r\nSalem is a Sr. Petroleum Economics Consultant with the National Oil Corporation, Tripoli, Libya. He has previously worked with Esso Standard Libya Inc., Sirte Oil Company, Agip Gas b. v.\r\nSalem has over 50 years of diversified experience in petroleum reservoir engineering, production operations, corporate planning and project economics. He had carried out a number of economic evaluation studies on multi-billion dollar oil and gas offshore field development projects.\r\nSalem is the co-author of several oil & gas reservoir simulation studies carried out at the Exxon Production Research Co. in Houston, Texas including the Sorra, Meghil and Lehib Dor-Marada fields studies. He is also the co-author of Libya gas production and utilization master plan.\r\nSalem developed and delivered \"Petroleum Project Economics & Risk Analysis\" course throughout North Africa, the Middle East and Europe for the past 25 years. These courses have been highly commended by the delegates and th', 'Petroleum Economics\r\nPetroleum Project Economics & Risk Analysis\r\nBasic Petroleum Technology\r\nEconomic Studies & Feasibility Evaluation\r\nOIL & GAS INDUSTRY', NULL, '', '+218924191940', 'salemzeglam@yahoo.com', '$2y$10$qFAI3tWJZAUPyf0UgeTPWuIYM71wkwFmQVvG2l.mZRtIPTRN6C4pq', NULL, 1, 3, 2, '68aae865d04d9.pdf', 'photo_678a6f498ad614.37766559.jpg', '', 'No details provided', '2025-08-07 12:45:59', '2025-08-24 04:24:37', 1, 'male', 0, 'pending', 'Advanced', 'Advanced'),
