(2676, '25-02-103-T2676', 59, 103, 345, 2, 1, '10', 0.00, '2025-07-29', 1, NULL, 'With the rapid advancement of digital transformation, programming has become an essential skill across various industries. This training program aims to build a solid foundational knowledge in computer programming by introducing participants to essential programming concepts, logical structuring of code, and problem-solving through computers. The program is highly practical to ensure better understanding and skill acquisition.', 'By the end of this program, participants will be able to:\r\n1.	Understand the fundamental concepts of programming and algorithms.\r\n2.	Write code using a modern programming language (e.g., Python, JavaScript, or PHP).\r\n3.	Develop simple programs involving inputs, outputs, and logical operations.\r\n4.	Apply Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) principles to build organized projects.\r\n5.	Connect programs to databases to develop real-world applications.\r\n6.	Gain skills in debugging and troubleshooting code.\r\n7.	Execute a simple programming project that combines all learned skills.\r\n', 'Computer Programmers\r\nWeb Designers', 'Day 1	Introduction to Programming	\r\n- What is programming and why is it important?\r\n- Overview of programming languages\r\n- Setting up the development environment (e.g., Python + VS Code)\r\n- Writing your first program (\"Hello World\")\r\n\r\nDay 2	Inputs, Variables & Data Types	\r\n- Storing data with variables\r\n- Data types (string, numeric, boolean, etc.)\r\n- Input/output statements\r\n- Hands-on practice with variables\r\n\r\nDay 3	Operators & Conditional Statements	\r\n- Arithmetic and logical operators\r\n- Conditional structures: if, else, elif\r\n- Practical exercises on decision making\r\n\r\nDay 4	Loops & Iterations	\r\n- for loops, while loops\r\n- Nested loops\r\n- Real-world loop-based programs\r\n\r\nDay 5	Functions	\r\n- Defining and using functions\r\n- Understanding code reusability and task separation\r\n- Built-in vs custom functions\r\n\r\nDay 6	Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)	\r\n- What is OOP?\r\n- Classes and objects\r\n- Concepts: inheritance, encapsulation, polymorphism\r\n\r\nDay 7	Files & Data Handling	\r\n- Opening, reading, writing text files\r\n- Using files in real applications like user logs\r\n\r\nDay 8	Introduction to Databases	\r\n- What is a database?\r\n- Basics of SQL\r\n- Connecting a program to a database\r\n\r\nDay 9	Debugging & Error Handling	\r\n- Types of errors in programming\r\n- Debugging tools and techniques\r\n- Writing clean and maintainable code\r\n\r\nDay 10	Final Project	- Define a simple project (e.g., address book, calculator, registration system)\r\n- Break down tasks\r\n- Code review and project presentation\r\n'),
